    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d404">

                <pb facs="0511" n="503" sameAs="frus:frus1941v07/pg503"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">823.796/150: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Ambassador in Peru</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Norweb</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-03-28T18:00:00-05:00">March 28, 1941—6 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>52. Your 91, March 26, 3 p.m.<anchor n="15" xml:id="d404-f1"/> Please express to
                    the President of Peru<anchor n="16" xml:id="d404-f2"/> on behalf of this
                    Government hearty concurrence in the position which the President of Peru has
                    taken to the effect that aviation services in this hemisphere should not be
                    operated by non-American interests. It is indeed gratifying to find this
                    position so definitely implemented by the cancellation by Peru of the
                        Lufthansa<anchor n="17" xml:id="d404-f3"/> contract. This action makes a
                    real contribution to continental solidarity and to continental defense.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Welles</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d404-f1" n="15" xml:id="d404-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d404-f2" n="16" xml:id="d404-f2-content">
                <p>Manuel Prado y Ugarteche.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d404-f3" n="17" xml:id="d404-f3-content">
                <p>German aviation company; its contract in Peru was cancelled on March 24.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
